From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] schedsvc, taskschd: task security descriptors, run times and running instances

These were E_NOTIMPL in both the schedule service and taskschd:

- Security descriptors: SchRpcGetSecurity/SetSecurity keep a task's or
  folder's descriptor where Windows keeps it (Schedule\TaskCache\Tree\<path>,
  value SD); a path never set gives the default (Administrators and SYSTEM
  full, Authenticated Users read/execute); bad SDDL is refused, a missing
  path is ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND. ITaskFolder and IRegisteredTask
  Get/SetSecurityDescriptor use them, and the sddl given to RegisterTask,
  RegisterTaskDefinition and CreateFolder (ignored before) is applied.
- Run times: SchRpcScheduledRuntimes walks the task's calendar triggers
  (time, daily, weekly) through the scheduler's own trigger arithmetic, in
  local time with that day's daylight saving; IRegisteredTask::NextRunTime
  (0 when there is none) and GetRunTimes (CoTaskMemAlloc'd array) use it.
- Missed runs: the scheduled times that fell between a task's last run
  (or its writing) and the scheduler's start.
- Running instances: a task started by the scheduler gets an instance
  GUID and keeps its action's command line and process id while it runs;
  SchRpcEnumInstances (of a task, a folder's tasks, or all),
  SchRpcGetInstanceInfo and SchRpcStopInstance answer from them; Run
  returns the instance. IRegisteredTask::GetInstances and
  ITaskService::GetRunningTasks give an IRunningTaskCollection (Count,
  one-based Item, _NewEnum); IRunningTask has its InstanceGuid,
  CurrentAction and EnginePID and stops its own instance. A person's tasks
  run in their own task host and are not listed by the service.
- The registered-task enumerator clones.

Wine's taskschd and schedsvc tests: no failures; a stale todo_wine in the
rpcapi test (EnableTask, already right) removed.

Gate: test/taskinfo-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_TASK_SECURITY (schedsvc/schedsvc.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_RUN_TIMES
(schedsvc/taskrun.c).
